{"step_index":1244,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:09:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-20T02:39:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-20T02:39:40+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/profitability.py`\nTotal Lines: 142\nTotal Bytes: 5672\nShowing lines 1 to 142\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: Profitability & economic modelling module.\n3: \n4: Converts operational telemetry into financial loss estimates and\n5: supports what-if scenario simulation via parameter sliders.\n6: \"\"\"\n7: from __future__ import annotations\n8: \n9: # Assumed unit revenue multiplier (material cost → selling price)\n10: # Adjust via sidebar — this is the default fallback\n11: _DEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER = 4.0\n12: \n13: \n14: def compute_financials(\n15:     analysis: dict | None,\n16:     defect_summary: dict | None,\n17:     scrap_cost_per_unit: float = 15.0,\n18:     downtime_cost_per_min: float = 2.50,\n19:     revenue_multiplier: float = _DEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER,\n20: ) -> dict:\n21:     \"\"\"\n22:     Compute financial KPIs from operational telemetry.\n23: \n24:     Parameters\n25:     ----------\n26:     analysis              Output of production_analyzer.analyze()\n27:     defect_summary        Output of DefectRegistry.summary()\n28:     scrap_cost_per_unit   Material cost lost per scrapped unit ($)\n29:     downtime_cost_per_min Cost of bottleneck idle time per minute ($)\n30:     revenue_multiplier    Selling price = scrap_cost × multiplier\n31: \n32:     Returns\n33:     -------\n34:     dict with financial KPIs (all in USD)\n35:     \"\"\"\n36:     if analysis is None:\n37:         return _empty_financials()\n38: \n39:     total_parts    = analysis.get('total_parts', 0)\n40:     demand         = analysis.get('demand', 0)\n41:     throughput_gap = analysis.get('throughput_gap', 0)\n42:     bn_wait        = analysis.get('bottleneck_wait', 0)   # avg wait (min) at bottleneck\n43: \n44:     defect_rate_pct = (defect_summary or {}).get('defect_rate', 0)   # 0-100\n45:     defect_rate     = defect_rate_pct / 100.0\n46: \n47:     # Units\n48:     good_units  = total_parts * (1 - defect_rate)\n49:     scrap_units = total_parts * defect_rate\n50: \n51:     # Unit revenue and rework cost estimates\n52:     unit_revenue = scrap_cost_per_unit * revenue_multiplier\n53:     rework_cost  = scrap_cost_per_unit * 0.4  # 40% of material cost to rework\n54: \n55:     # ── Loss components ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56:     scrap_material_loss = scrap_units * scrap_cost_per_unit\n57:     bottleneck_idle_loss = bn_wait * downtime_cost_per_min   # per simulation run\n58:     opportunity_loss    = throughput_gap * unit_revenue      # revenue missed from unmet demand\n59:     rework_cost_total   = scrap_units * rework_cost * 0.3    # assume 30% reworked, rest scrapped\n60: \n61:     total_loss = scrap_material_loss + bottleneck_idle_loss + opportunity_loss + rework_cost_total\n62: \n63:     # ── Revenue / Margin ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64:     gross_revenue = good_units * unit_revenue\n65:     net_margin    = gross_revenue - total_loss\n66:     margin_pct    = (net_margin / gross_revenue * 100) if gross_revenue > 0 else 0\n67: \n68:     return {\n69:         'total_parts':          round(total_parts, 1),\n70:         'good_units':           round(good_units, 1),\n71:         'scrap_units':          round(scrap_units, 1),\n72:         'defect_rate_pct':      round(defect_rate_pct, 2),\n73:         'gross_revenue':        round(gross_revenue, 2),\n74:         'scrap_loss':           round(scrap_material_loss, 2),\n75:         'bottleneck_idle_loss': round(bottleneck_idle_loss, 2),\n76:         'opportunity_loss':     round(opportunity_loss, 2),\n77:         'rework_cost':          round(rework_cost_total, 2),\n78:         'total_loss':           round(total_loss, 2),\n79:         'net_margin':           round(net_margin, 2),\n80:         'margin_pct':           round(margin_pct, 1),\n81:     }\n82: \n83: \n84: def what_if(\n85:     analysis: dict | None,\n86:     defect_summary: dict | None,\n87:     scrap_cost_per_unit: float,\n88:     downtime_cost_per_min: float,\n89:     util_improvement_pct: float = 0.0,\n90:     scrap_reduction_pct: float = 0.0,\n91:     revenue_multiplier: float = _DEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER,\n92: ) -> dict:\n93:     \"\"\"\n94:     Simulate the financial impact of process improvements.\n95: \n96:     Parameters\n97:     ----------\n98:     util_improvement_pct   % reduction in bottleneck waiting time (0-100)\n99:     scrap_reduction_pct    % reduction in defect rate (0-100)\n100:     \"\"\"\n101:     if analysis is None:\n102:         return _empty_financials()\n103: \n104:     # Clone and adjust analysis\n105:     adj_analysis = dict(analysis)\n106:     adj_analysis['bottleneck_wait']     = analysis['bottleneck_wait']     * (1 - util_improvement_pct / 100)\n107:     adj_analysis['throughput_gap']      = analysis['throughput_gap']      * (1 - util_improvement_pct / 100)\n108: \n109:     # Clone and adjust defect summary\n110:     base_rate = (defect_summary or {}).get('defect_rate', 0)\n111:     adj_defect = dict(defect_summary) if defect_summary else {}\n112:     adj_defect['defect_rate'] = base_rate * (1 - scrap_reduction_pct / 100)\n113: \n114:     return compute_financials(\n115:         adj_analysis, adj_defect,\n116:         scrap_cost_per_unit, downtime_cost_per_min,\n117:         revenue_multiplier,\n118:     )\n119: \n120: \n121: def impact_delta(baseline: dict, whatif: dict) -> dict:\n122:     \"\"\"Compute absolute and relative improvement from baseline to what-if.\"\"\"\n123:     delta_margin = whatif['net_margin'] - baseline['net_margin']\n124:     delta_loss   = baseline['total_loss'] - whatif['total_loss']\n125:     return {\n126:         'delta_margin':     round(delta_margin, 2),\n127:         'delta_loss_saved': round(delta_loss, 2),\n128:         'margin_improvement_pct': round(\n129:             delta_margin / abs(baseline['net_margin']) * 100\n130:             if baseline['net_margin'] != 0 else 0, 1\n131:         ),\n132:     }\n133: \n134: \n135: def _empty_financials() -> dict:\n136:     keys = [\n137:         'total_parts', 'good_units', 'scrap_units', 'defect_rate_pct',\n138:         'gross_revenue', 'scrap_loss', 'bottleneck_idle_loss',\n139:         'opportunity_loss', 'rework_cost', 'total_loss', 'net_margin', 'margin_pct',\n140:     ]\n141:     return {k: 0 for k in keys}\n142: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1243,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:09:22Z","content":"Let me first study the current code structure deeply before building anything:","thinking":"The user wants two major features:\n1. Animated Production Line Simulator - a moving flowchart/Sankey diagram showing parts flowing through stations based on Arena data, with bottlenecks pulsing red\n2. 3D Surface Plot for What-If - a 3D surface showing margin changes across scrap reduction vs downtime improvement\n\nAnd also make the website more classy overall.\n\nThis is a significant feature addition. Let me plan this carefully:\n\n1. **Animated Production Line Simulator**: \n   - This should be built using Plotly's animation capabilities or a custom HTML/JS animation\n   - For the Sankey/flowchart: I can use Plotly Sankey with animated frames, or build a custom SVG/HTML animation\n   - I'm deciding between a Plotly animated figure with frame objects versus a custom HTML/CSS/JS component injected via Streamlit's HTML component, and I think a custom canvas animation would best capture parts visibly flowing through stations. I'll build a production flow animation function that uses station names, utilization percentages, waiting times, and throughput data to drive the visualization.\n\nNext I'm designing a 3D surface plot for the what-if scenario, mapping scrap reduction and utilization improvement percentages against net margin, computed by running the what_if function across a grid, and I'll package this as a margin_surface_3d function alongside the flow chart. I also want to make the website feel more polished with refined typography, glassmorphism effects, and smoother color transitions, so I should first review the app's current state closely.\n\nFor the animated production line, I'm planning to use Streamlit's HTML component to embed a custom canvas animation showing particles flowing between stations, with node colors reflecting utilization levels and bottlenecks pulsing red.\n\nFor the 3D surface plot, I'll add a function to chart_helpers.py that generates a grid of what-if scenarios across defect rate, scrap cost, downtime cost, and revenue multiplier, then renders it as a Plotly surface. Before implementing, I want to check the existing code structure first.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\modules\\profitability.py","toolAction":"Viewing profitability module","toolSummary":"Profitability module review"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\app.py","EndLine":820,"StartLine":740,"toolAction":"Viewing Tab 2 production section","toolSummary":"Production tab area"}}]}
