uto-loader + model session state init\n  - Lines 648–738: Sidebar (weights input, dataset uploader tabs, economic sliders)\n  - Lines 740–820: Header KPI strip + HUD banner\n  - Lines 820–826: Tab definitions (tab1–tab5)\n  - Lines 983–1074: **Tab 2** — production flow, static SCADA flowchart at 1009–1029, bottleneck card at 1031–1062, charts at 1060–1062, multi-model benchmark at 1064–1074\n  - Lines 1140–1280: Tab 4 (What-If) — sliders, financial KPIs, `margin_comparison_bar` call at ~1258\n\n- **`modules/profitability.py`** (142 lines total):\n  - `compute_financials()` lines 14–81 — all financial KPI calculation\n  - `what_if()` lines 84–118 — takes `util_improvement_pct` and `scrap_reduction_pct`, adjusts analysis dict and defect summary, calls `compute_financials()`\n  - `impact_delta()` lines 121–132\n\n- **`utils/chart_helpers.py`** (464 lines total):\n  - Lines 1–52: palette `_CYBER` dict, `_BG`, `_base_layout()`\n  - Lines 54–247: Quality charts (donut, bar, histogram, trend)\n  - Lines 150–245: Production flow charts (utilization_bar, waiting_time_bar, radar)\n  - Lines 248–327: **Financial charts** — `financial_waterfall()` at 250, `margin_comparison_bar()` at 282\n  - Lines 329–424: ANN charts (gauge, sweep, validation scatter)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n### Immediate Task\nThe user's most recent request (still fully unimplemented):\n> *\"Animated Production Line Simulator — A moving flowchart/Sankey diagram that shows parts flowing through stations in real-time based on Arena data. Bottlenecks pulse red. 3D Surface Plot for What-If — Instead of flat bar charts — a 3D surface showing how margin changes across two variables simultaneously (e.g. scrap reduction vs downtime improvement). can we do this and make the website more classy\"*\n\n### Implementation Plan\n\n**Step 1 — Add `production_flow_animation()` to `chart_helpers.py`**\n- New function at the end of the Production Flow Charts section (~line 248)\n- Takes `station_metrics: dict`, `bottleneck_station: str`, `model_name: str`\n- Uses `st.components.v1.html()` pattern — returns raw HTML string with embedded JS/CSS\n- Design: Dark background, SVG nodes for each station colored by utilization (green < 70%, orange 70–85%, red > 85%), CSS keyframe animation for flowing particles (small dots) along path lines between nodes, bottleneck node has `animation: pulse 1s infinite` with red glow\n- Data already available from `analysis['stations']` in Tab 2\n\n**Step 2 — Add `margin_surface_3d()` to `chart_helpers.py`**  \n- New function after `margin_comparison_bar()` (~line 327)\n- Parameters: `analysis, defect_summary, scrap_cost, downtime_cost, revenue_mult`\n- Internally: build `np.linspace(0, 50, 30)` grid for scrap_reduction, `np.linspace(0, 30, 30)` for util_improvement\n- Call `what_if()` for each combination → extract `net_margin`\n- Build `Z` matrix, plot `go.Surface` with colorscale `'Viridis'`\n- Axes: X = \"Scrap Reduction %\", Y = \"Utilization Improvement %\", Z = \"Net Margin ($)\"\n\n**Step 3 — Wire both into app.py**\n- Tab 2: Replace or augment the static `flow_html` block (lines 1009–1029) — add animated simulator below the existing static strip OR replace it entirely using `st.components.v1.html()`\n- Tab 4: Add `st.plotly_chart(margin_surface_3d(...))` below or alongside the existing `margin_comparison_bar` chart\n\n**Step 4 — CSS polish pass**\n- Refine global CSS: deeper glassmorphism on cards, smoother border gradients, tab label styling, section header typography\n\n### Next Agent Should\n1. Read `app.py` lines 1009–1029 (static flowchart) and lines 1250–1270 (what-if chart block) to see exact insertion points\n2. Read `utils/chart_helpers.py` lines 248–327 to see where to insert new functions\n3. Implement `production_flow_animation()` as an HTML component in `chart_helpers.py`\n4. Implement `margin_surface_3d()` as a Plotly Surface in `chart_helpers.py`\n5. Import and wire both into `app.py` at the correct tab locations\n6. Run `python -m py_compile app.py utils/chart_helpers.py` to verify\n7. Do a CSS polish pass in the CSS block (app.py lines ~42–480)\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789840749044]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/.user_uploaded/media_1789840749044.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T17:59:23Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: architecture]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/architecture.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T19:42:35Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T18:03:55Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: walkthrough]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/walkthrough.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T19:04:30Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: this summary is just for your reference. You may respond to my previous and future messages, but DO NOT ACKNOWLEDGE THIS CHECKPOINT MESSAGE. JUST READ IT BUT DO NOT MENTION IT, RESPOND TO IT, OR TAKE ACTION BECAUSE OF IT.**"}
